{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1436707-dragon-making-wyrm-antagonists","id":1436707,"title":"[Dragon] Making Wyrm antagonists","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-02-23T11:23:05-08:00","id":1436707,"title":"[Dragon] Making Wyrm antagonists","content":"So I want the <b>Dragon</b> enemy to put against my <b>Origin</b>-to-<b>Hero</b> players. ( I think defeting this Dragon will be their last step to become Heroes. ) I just cannot guess what rules to use for it - Origin Antagonists, Hero Antagonists, Dragon particular PCs rules? Make him as Heir or Lesser Wyrm? <b>What would be your advise on this antagonists power level for 5-6 PCs of late Origin tier?</b><br /> <br /> Idea for my particular Wyrm is Joka or Lindwurm that collect art pieces in Louvre as his/her personal Treasure, under his/her guard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-23-2021, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-23T11:35:49-08:00","id":1436710,"title":"","content":"This is what happens when players use different rules from everyone else in a game.<br /> <br /> That said, it's Origin so you want to balanced for Origin level. Use Origin antagonists and borrow from other sources as needed to get what you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-23T12:11:25-08:00","id":1436714,"title":"","content":"My suggestion is to make them as a Origin Antagonist and pick some qualities related to dragons, inspired in the Repitilian Destroyers from Dragon (page 33 from the big manuscript).<br /> <br /> Edit: making them as a Hero antagonist will give more qualities (as far as I recall) for the same dice pool. It may be useful if you want more magical power and less brutish might.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-23T12:19:23-08:00","id":1436716,"title":"","content":"I'd go with something like a Rival from the Hero book, maybe a Nemesis if your Origin characters are fairly tough. A basilisk from the example antagonists in the Hero book might work well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-23T12:44:33-08:00","id":1436722,"title":"","content":"I wanted this antagonist to be more 'shadow enemy behind whole Louvre' and center piece of the story - but maybe not so direct powerful as typical <i>Monster</i> from <b>Origin</b>, in the end. So maybe base him on <i>Nemesis</i> from <b>Hero</b>? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1436707-dragon-making-wyrm-antagonists?p=1436714#post1436714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(page 33 from the big manuscript).</div> </div> </div> </div>Forgotten there is one big compiled manuscript now - downloading both of <b>Dragon</b> and <b>Masks of Mythos</b> of mine books. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-24-2021, 12:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-27T08:08:22-08:00","id":1437234,"title":"","content":"Here is my first take on Dragon antagonists. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24985_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24985\" data-vbnamecard=\"24985\">Mateus Luz</a>, especially your opinion I'm interested.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Ladon, Garden of the Hesperides Dragon</b></span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/6Zmpp5V.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This \u2018Ladon\u2019 is the greater Heir of the legendary dragon from Garden of the Hesperides, that guarded Golden Apples of Hera in there. This Heir is now curator of one of major art museums, where he guards most of it\u2019s collection \u2013 especially Theoi Relics he is very fond off.<br /> <br /> d \u2013 Material from <b>Scion: Dragon</b><br /> o \u2013 Material from <b>Origin</b> book<br /> h \u2013 Material from <b>Hero</b> book<br /> * \u2013 See below<br /> <b>Archetype:</b> Nemesis ( Dragon Heir )<br /> <b>Flight:</b> Lindwurms ( Eastern, Greek branch )<br /> <b>Quality: </b>Mystic Arsenal h ( Relics collection ), Mother\u2019s Child d, The Old Destroyer d, Render d, Heavily Armored o ( Hard 2, Soft 1 ), Cross-Training o ( Many Heads, many actions )<br /> <b>Flairs:</b> ?<br /> <b>Drive:</b> To protect his \u2018Hoard\u2019 ( i.e. museum collection )<br /> <b>Weakness:</b> <b>Hesperides Guardian</b> \u2013 When seeing any apple or apple-shaped objects, Ladon stops for one turn \u2013 and if not seeing part of his Hoard stolen \u2013 will defend 'apples'.<br /> <b>Primary Pool (11):</b> Athletics, Close Combat, Arts &amp; Relics<br /> <b>Secondary Pool (9):</b> Dragon Magic, Dragon Intrigues, Firearms<br /> <b>Desperation Pool</b>: 6<br /> <b>Speed: </b>15<br /> <b>Health:</b> 5 ( 7 with Hard Armor )<br /> <b>Defense</b>: 4 ( 5 with Soft Armor )<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 9<br /> <b>Attacks:</b><br /> <b><i>Claws </i></b>- Enhancement 2, Natural, Range: Close, Lethal, Messy, Piercing<br /> <b><i>Jaws </i></b>- Enhancement 2, Natural, Piercing, Grapple, Range: Close, Lethal, Messy, Piercing<br /> <b><i>Desert Eagle -</i></b> Enhancement 2, Natural, Range: Medium, Lethal","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-24-2021, 05:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-27T10:22:34-08:00","id":1437244,"title":"","content":"Beautiful! Great big boss to fight to get a golden apple! Could be an adversary to low legend Heroes too.<br /> <br /> Now, my opinion that may diverge is: Ladon was a challenge to Hercules in his demigod period, what means he should be more powerful. But it looks great as a reincarnating Ladon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-27T10:53:24-08:00","id":1437250,"title":"","content":"Looks like this is a heir of Ladon that took the dragon's name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T23:59:50-07:00","id":1445623,"title":"","content":"Other Dragon related Antagonist idea - <b>What could be Dragon related 'titanspawn', so to speak? </b>Like Dinosaurs can work as 'titanspawn' category? Some 'wyrms' beings? Other ideas could you point for Dragon-related beings, but also not 'full power' as proper Dragons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T06:56:22-07:00","id":1448978,"title":"","content":"<b>How to stat proper Dragon-dragon-like serpentine monster for Scions to fight with?</b> I want to stat Ry\u016bjin, the Dragon King Incarnation for PCs to fight with. Should it be stated as Wyrm from <b>Dragon</b>, Titanspawn from <b>Hero</b> book - or other Archetype? <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24985_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24985\" data-vbnamecard=\"24985\">Mateus Luz</a>, what do you think mechanically?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"https://images-wixmp-ed30a86b8c4ca887773594c2.wixmp.com/f/6f2b45d7-ba80-4f0a-a622-6d93aba7b771/d4w6866-60f8e0f3-985a-40c0-8da1-6f6c990187d0.jpg?token=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..06t2O__HSFaL6LJhSkJp3eH5T1LnyOUGKBKugcZhwMo\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T07:25:36-07:00","id":1448982,"title":"","content":"Well... most of the famous dragons were killed by or defeated Gods and Demigods, so real Wyrms, the big ones, are just too big to deal with on heroic level, at least in direct combat.<br /> <br /> If you want to interact with it, maybe you should use the Goliath rules from Demigod (Demigod big manuscript page 257), much like I would do to face a god. Make it scale 6+ and define how much the dragon is trying to kill you actively (in opposition to kill you by mistake when step in a building or something with you inside).<br /> <br /> This system keep the fight to last longer, even several sessions, while the characters have a chance to die, it\u2019s not instakill. It definitely worth the reading!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 05-19-2021, 10:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T10:25:09-07:00","id":1451349,"title":"","content":"I'm preparing the Greater Wyrm as my mid-chronicle bigger boss, that probably will survive players and will then run away. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1450307-dragon-wyrms-incarnations?p=1450451#post1450451\">It's 'reincarnation' of J\u00f6rmungandr</a> - and is probably to survive 3-5 Hero PCs and run away after it, to span intrugie more in chronicle. Here are stats I prepared for it. Comments are welcome - especially from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24985_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24985\" data-vbnamecard=\"24985\">Mateus Luz</a> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> - it's my first NPC made with Heirs rules from <b>Scion Dragon</b> book.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>J\u00f6rmungandr Greater Wyrm ( Reincarnation )</b></span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/FzRQqHS.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Sophie is more resolute incarnation of J\u00f6rmungandr, concerned more with ruling and destruction of enemies \u2013 than collecting and traveling. She was raised in small town or suburbia \u2013 and risen in ranks of local government administration. She is own Mayor\u2019s Assistant, true power behind the throne of local community.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Draconic Form</b></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/tMVd5RU.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Name:</b> Sophie Jensen<br /> <b>Flight:</b> Lindwurm (J\u00f6rmungandr)<br /> <b>Inheritance:</b> 10 ( Greater Wyrm* ) *<b>Greater Wyrm</b> is fan name on Inheritance 10 Heirs, that are physical \u2018incarnations\u2019 of their Patron Dragon.<br /> <b>Callings:</b> Destroyer 4, Ruler 3, Collector 3, Nomad 1<br /> <b>Memory:</b> Icy cold waters and crushing depths; sun warmed beaches with sea birds circling<br /> overhead; the sight of the world from above, as one circles it; a low burning hatred fueled by<br /> embarrassment and apathy.<br /> <b>Dragon Magic:</b> Elemental Manipulation (Frost, Water), Flight, Understanding, Weather Control, Lindwurm<br /> <b>Paths: </b><br /> <b>Origin:</b> <i>Always Watched</i> ( Academics, Integrity, Subterfuge ) \u2013 3rd<br /> <b>Role:</b> <i>Mayor\u2019s Assistant</i> ( Empathy, Leadership, Persuasion ) \u2013 1st<br /> <b>Flight:</b> <i>Lindwurms</i> (Close Combat, Survival, Persuasion ) \u2013 2nd<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 3, Athletics (Swimming) 3, Close Combat 3, Culture 1, Empathy 3, Integrity (Hiding Intentions) 3, Leadership 3, Occult 2, Persuasion 5, Subterfuge (Lies) 3, Survival 2, Technology ( Office works ) 1<br /> <b>Attributes: </b>(Finesse Approach) Intellect 3, Cunning 4, Resolve 5, Might 3, Dexterity 5, Stamina 5, Presence 4, Manipulation 5, Composure 3<br /> <b>Calling Knacks:</b> Infinite Pockets, Armor-Shearing Jaws, Enhanced Impact, Terrible Dragon Roar + Render of Cities, Invulnerable Master, Invoke Anger, Loyal Servant, Perfect Poise + Fearless Presence, Friends Anywhere \u2013 11 in Sum<br /> <b>Dragon Knacks:</b> Scent the Divine \u2013 11 in Sum + Scent the Divine<br /> <b>Knacks of Scale </b>- Unstoppable Force, On My Command ( calling a whole city to aid ), Insatiable Collector<br /> <b>Transformation Knacks </b>- Bottomless Lungs, Brutal Might, Devastating Dragon\u2019s Presence, Dragon\u2019s Breath, Eel\u2019s Trickery, Great Slithering Bulk, Rending Claws, Dragon\u2019s Scales<br /> <b>Dragon Spells</b> - 11 in Sum<br /> Elemental Manipulation (Frost) - Cool Down, Flash Freeze, Rime<br /> Elemental Manipulation (Water) - Flash Flood<br /> Understanding - Foresight, Piercing Gaze<br /> Weather Control - Alter Weather, Lethal Weather, Localized Weather, Resist Weather<br /> Lindwurms - Avarice - Irresistible Craving<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T05:38:30-07:00","id":1452147,"title":"","content":"I liked a lot the idea, She seams very powerful and amazing, a worth final enemy for a band of Demigods, and her size scale must be 6+ at least in her dragon form.<br /> <br /> She must be a worth enemy to Thor, and I think she killed him with her poison, I am not sure how she uses it, so I guess the Dragon Breath could fit it nicely. Now, to really know if it fits as an enemy for a god, we need God, so...<br /> <br /> I honestly would make her a Goliath (as I would do for any god level adversary), but it\u2019s my personal opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T05:50:57-07:00","id":1452150,"title":"","content":"Hmm, Demigods you say... Not something for Heroes of Legend 1 that need to run from it, seeing how powerful she is? I need PCs be forced to seek help in defeating her with Gods of Pantheons - but that she would not instant kill them... \ud83e\udd14","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-14-2021, 09:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T16:25:25-07:00","id":1452251,"title":"","content":"She can kill them almost instantly if in Dragon form. Dragon form gain scale, in that case a lot is scale....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T23:38:40-07:00","id":1452283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1436707-dragon-making-wyrm-antagonists?p=1452251#post1452251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She can kill them almost instantly if in Dragon form. Dragon form gain scale, in that case a lot is scale....</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... So lowering Inheritance to like 5 would make it only Scale +3 =&gt; not something that kills instantly as I read rules correctly, yes?<br /> <br /> Rules seems to imply Heir get's ONLY +1 Scale, not '+1 Scale per two dots of Inheritance'... <b>Draconic Form</b><br /><br /><ul><li><i>The Heir gains +1 Scale on all actions, which doesn\u2019t stack with any Scale benefits from Knacks or other sources; if two sources would grant Scale, use the highest bonus among them.</i></li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-15-2021, 02:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T02:13:02-07:00","id":1452295,"title":"","content":"I may be wrong, but I think the rules for Lesser Wyrms increase this Scale lift. I don\u2019t have the manuscript on me now, unfortunately.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T03:56:45-07:00","id":1452442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1436707-dragon-making-wyrm-antagonists?p=1452295#post1452295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may be wrong, but I think the rules for Lesser Wyrms increase this Scale lift. I don\u2019t have the manuscript on me now, unfortunately.</div> </div> </div> </div>Checked quickly on Manuscript on 'Lesser Wyrms' term...<br /> <br /> P. 8:<br /> <i>\u2022 Lesser Wyrm: An Heir who has an Inheritance rating of 5 or more. Lesser Wyrms are Tier 2 characters and embody more of their draconic side than their human side. </i><br /> <br /> P. 249:<br /> <i>\u2022 A Lesser Wyrm is more comfortable in her draconic form than in her human one. She is no longer limited to transforming into her draconic form once per scene, and can switch back and forth as many times as she likes. At Inheritance 9, the Heir fully transforms into her draconic form. She can now imbue an Inheritance to take on her human form in reverse of what she could do before. While in a human form, she cannot activate any of her Transformation Knacks that would show her draconic side, though she can use her Knacks of Scale. When using a Knack of Scale, failure to buy off the True Draconic Nature Complication results in ending the human form transformation.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Feats of Scale are bigger and more showy for Lesser Wyrms than other Heirs. When a Lesser Wyrm performs a Feat of Scale, she can spend a Momentum to gain an additional +1 Scale for the action regardless of if the action falls in line with her Deed Name. This does stack with the Deed Name Scale bonus though. But, doing so increases her cumulative Complication for True Draconic Nature by +1. </i><br /> <br /> So going with base +1 Scale for Draconic Form of any Heir, and +1 Scale for Lesser Wyrms and +1 Scale from Deed Name =&gt; Max Lesser Wyrms can get +3 Scale. Or so is my rules reading now...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-16-2021, 07:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T05:46:20-07:00","id":1452453,"title":"","content":"Suddenly they seam to fit as final boss in a heroes campaign. I was sure there was something to make them gain a lot of scale easily, but I am probably wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T07:00:41-07:00","id":1452470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1436707-dragon-making-wyrm-antagonists?p=1452453#post1452453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Suddenly they seam to fit as final boss in a heroes campaign. I was sure there was something to make them gain a lot of scale easily, but I am probably wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe some random powers? One of Draconic Knacks or Spells maybe adds next Scale?<br /> <br /> Either way - with Scale +3 on attacks,<i> <b>J\u00f6rmungandr Greater Wyrm</b>( Reincarnation )</i> does not seems as such overkill, yes? PCs on Legend 1 should - bearly - survive fight with her? Or is she still too powerfull on Inheritance 10, maybe?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T09:36:00-07:00","id":1452492,"title":"","content":"Hard to tell. I think a group of high legend Heroes could defeat as described. Not sure... Honestly I never tried to play with dragons so far, so I don\u2019t know how powerful they really can be. I haven\u2019t even built one to try...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T11:53:45-07:00","id":1452514,"title":"","content":"Correctly me if i'm wrong - Heroes with Legend 1-5 have Scale +1 for some things in combat, yes?<br /> <br /> Dragon even with Scale +3 ( that you may go only by invoking Deed Name ) has only Scale +2 over Heroes on Legend 1.<br /> <br /> And Scale +2 is getting +4 Enhancment for the Dragon on the attacks - so it would 'only' mean that on normal attack pools, it gets extra Injury, from <i>Critical </i>(4s) Stunt.<br /> <br /> So if <i>Lesser Wyrms</i> normally doing 1-2 Injury per attack - with it's Scale +2 over Heroes, it will only get to 2-3 Injuries. Enough to 'hit hard' Legend 1 characters - but not instant kill in first attack. Am I right on those approximations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-17-2021, 02:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T12:07:02-07:00","id":1452515,"title":"","content":"Heroes can raise their scale by \u00bd legend round up, and they are limited to legend 4, but they are limited to one action per legend spent, what is pretty limiting. Also this increase in scale is just related to the title, so some of the heroes may have some issue to raise that much, limited to no more than +1 scale.<br /> <br /> So a band of Heroes facing a Scale 3 dragon will have a hard time to keep all characters alive for more than a few rounds, when they get out of legend and can\u2019t stand a chance against the overwhelming scale.<br /> <br /> But yes, your approximations are right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T20:51:34-07:00","id":1452735,"title":"","content":"The problem with that is Heirs/Lesser Wyrms have a similar ability that can give them 1/2 their Inheritance in Scale under some circumstances, (knack dependant, I think). Given the general rule about replacing Scale, rather than adding it.<br /> Plus the statement about being tier 2 is a typo, lesser Wyrms are tier 3 and greater ones are tier 4.<br /> <br /> And don't forget that Lesser Wyrms get a cost reduction on their Spells","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-03T10:02:39-07:00","id":1454139,"title":"","content":"5 Heroes on Legend 1 easily mooped my <i><b>J\u00f6rmungandr Greater Wyrm </b></i>without large problems. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ( Only one PC got somehow beaten by 3 Injury levels. ) I forgot on Scale difference on two first attacks, but one of players generated like +4 Enhancement for all the Scions ( Leader Calling etc. ). Even with Scale difference later on, they just beated it by numbers alone. ( Previous Reptile Infiltrators bodyguards where more or less enemies on turn or two. )<br /> <br /> Clearly, <i><b>J\u00f6rmungandr Wyrm </b></i>should have regenerative abilities - as just 5 Heroes on one Wyrm just will defeat it easily. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1436707-dragon-making-wyrm-antagonists?p=1452735#post1452735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus the statement about being tier 2 is a typo, lesser Wyrms are tier 3 and greater ones are tier 4.</div> </div> </div> </div>So if Scions with Legend 1 are only Tier 1 - that means Greater Wyrms have Tier 4 - it means it should have +/- 6 Enhancement to things from Scale?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-04-2021, 01:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-04T02:33:20-07:00","id":1454184,"title":"","content":"Advice I got from Scion Discord on the Demigod level antagonists that should be real series bosses.<br /> 0. HEROES HAVE SCALE 0 ( unless powers )!!!!<br /> 1. Give it Passive Scale 4 all the time. Just. All the time, due to Size. Scale 4 will give like 8 Enhancement that breaks the Enhancement Cap. The Shockwave would hit most of the party with each attack. Scale 4 also will give a Defense Boost (also make sure your Antagonists have static defense)<br /> 2. Give it multiple Segments, each one with its own health bar and maybe keying certain powers to each Segment.<br /> 3. Remember that at that level, count 7 and up on the dice as successes.<br /> 4. Use 1 Tension to declare that the antagonist didn't DIE die, and got away to lick their wounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-04-2021, 01:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-04T05:20:52-07:00","id":1454190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1436707-dragon-making-wyrm-antagonists?p=1454139#post1454139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5 Heroes on Legend 1 easily mooped my <i><b>J\u00f6rmungandr Greater Wyrm </b></i>without large problems. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ( Only one PC got somehow beaten by 3 Injury levels. ) I forgot on Scale difference on two first attacks, but one of players generated like +4 Enhancement for all the Scions ( Leader Calling etc. ). Even with Scale difference later on, they just beated it by numbers alone. ( Previous Reptile Infiltrators bodyguards where more or less enemies on turn or two. )<br /> <br /> Clearly, <i><b>J\u00f6rmungandr Wyrm </b></i>should have regenerative abilities - as just 5 Heroes on one Wyrm just will defeat it easily. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So if Scions with Legend 1 are only Tier 1 - that means Greater Wyrms have Tier 4 - it means it should have +/- 6 Enhancement to things from Scale?</div> </div> </div> </div>Tiers don't actually interact with the scale system if I recall correctly. What they do is change the threshold for success; the 'target number'.<br /> Your Heroes need to roll 8's or higher for Successes.<br /> Your Greater Wyrm only needs to roll 7's. That is straight up 10% more succeses from any given dicepool.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-04T06:39:15-07:00","id":1454197,"title":"","content":"FallenEco is right, you don\u2019t compare tier to define scale or anything similar, scale is scale and tier is tier.<br /> <br /> But the tier has a connection to scale that is Legend/Inheritance, that can provide a good amount of scale with easy in the case of godlike creatures.<br /> <br /> So far we don\u2019t have god rules or anything similar, but taking Demigods and a lesser Wyrms as reference, greater wyrms are probably capable of maintain a high scale in a permanent fashion with little to no effort, if not by size and psysical might, by magic.<br /> <br /> How much scale? Well, scale 6 is kind of the up limit in Demigods, so I guess they will keep that way in God, and so to Greater Wyrms. And scale 6 means overwhelming to anything under scale 4\u2026 so, any hero and most of the demigods would have issues to deal with directly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-04T10:25:48-07:00","id":1454213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1436707-dragon-making-wyrm-antagonists?p=1454197#post1454197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So far we don\u2019t have god rules or anything similar, but taking Demigods and a lesser Wyrms as reference, greater wyrms are probably capable of maintain a high scale in a permanent fashion with little to no effort, if not by size and psysical might, by magic.<br /> <br /> How much scale? Well, scale 6 is kind of the up limit in Demigods, so I guess they will keep that way in God, and so to Greater Wyrms. And scale 6 means overwhelming to anything under scale 4\u2026 so, any hero and most of the demigods would have issues to deal with directly.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we go with Passive Scale ( i.e. Scale on anything ) as Demigod level Antagonist, I would rather see this as Passive Scale 4 level - enough to squash mere Heroes easily, but giving fighting chances on Demigods characters. ( As they can rose to Scales up to 3 with good powers. ) Passive Scale 6 would be true Gods area - so as 'Inheritance 11' Dragons, i.e. Dragon 'Gods'/Patrons of the book. But it's only my gut feeling, not supported by mechanical tests in game.<br /> <br /> Remember that Dragons also gats Scale +1 from Deed Name and various Draconic Knacks - then Passive Scale would be 4, with added +2 Scale with a well-chosen action (to working Scale 6 on particular action ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-04-2021, 01:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-04T10:56:10-07:00","id":1454218,"title":"","content":"Yes and no\u2026 Yes for the level you want to put the be adversaries of your characters, no to the fact they are bellow gods. The true dragons are absolutely powerful, they are match to gods, just take a look in who they kill or fight, Thor dies by the venon of one, another took an entire pantheon to defeat (with no causalities) and the weak ones protect stuff from gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}